                "complementary": "As a result, the text may be difficult or impossible to read for users with low vision or color blindness.\n##### Recommendation\nVerify that the text has sufficient contrast relative to all parts of the visually adjacent image content. For complex images, apply a solid background color to the text element to ensure that it has sufficient contrast, for example, using white text with a black background overlaid on the image. The contrast ratio must be at least 4.5:1 for normal text (smaller than 18pt/24px, or 14pt/18.5px for bold text), or 3:1 for larger text.\n##### Resources\n[Understanding Success Criterion 1.4.3: Contrast (Minimum)](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html)",
