                "title": "Link text contains the word \"click\"",
                "description": "One or more links contain the word \"click\".",
                "complementary": "This suggests that the link text may not be descriptive enough. Link text that simply says \"Click here\" (or similar) does not convey any useful information to assistive technology users as to the destination or purpose of the link. Link text that says something like \"Click here to view our Terms and Conditions\" is unnecessarily verbose, since users already know that links are activated by \"clicking\".\n##### Recommendation\nEnsure that link text clearly and uniquely describes the destination or purpose of the link, without using generic text such as \"click here\" or \"view more\". Link text should make sense out of context, so that a user can understand the purpose of the link without reference to the surrounding content.\n##### Resources\n[Link Text and Appearance](https://webaim.org/techniques/hypertext/link_text)",
                "gen4logics": [
                    "links"
                ]
            },
